{
  "TRANSACTION - FUNCTIONAL DESCRIPTION": "Obtains information about the pricing rule. Allows you to filter by various parameters.",
  "EXECUTION FLOWS - DETAILED DESCRIPTION": "The transaction obtains the pricingRuleId input and, when it is negative, adds warning ABKO00000050, returns an empty pricingRules list, and finishes without invoking the library. Otherwise, it builds a PricingRuleGetFilterParams object with all input filters, including pricing rule, date, activity, segment, settlement, active, pagination, type, status, attribute description, and attribute name. It invokes ABKOR000.executeGetPricingRules with the filter object and assigns the returned DataPricingRuleGet to dataOfPricingRules. If the returned pricingRules list is empty, it adds warning ABKO00000040. The resulting data and pagination information are returned in dataOfPricingRules.",
